 "notes": "Answers: dates any common shape (printed mmddyyyy in the boxes). fein '12-3456789' and 10-digit US phones, printed digit by digit in the form's cells (an EIN starting with 9 is printed as given, dash included, since its bare digits look like an ITIN to the writer). non_employees 'No' or 'Yes: services they perform'. ui_quarter: year first, '2026 Q3' (or an ISO date of the first $300 quarter, '2026-07-15'). acquired: 'No' or 'Yes: all|part, date, prior registration number, prior FEIN, prior legal name, prior address'. entity_change: 'No' or 'Yes: date, prior registration number, prior FEIN'. Addresses 'street, City, ST ZIP[, Country]' (county is left blank: the answers don't carry it). records_location and agent_address: one item per line or ';' - records: address; contact name; phone as 212-555-0134. agent: C/O name; address; phone; contact name. owners: one per line 'Name, Title, residence address and phone' (the SSN column is never written; the signer writes it). location_address: 'street, City, ST ZIP'. establishment: 'type of establishment, principal product or service, percent of revenue' (no commas inside each part). signer: 'Official position, phone, email'. The form's 'Group2' radio is one group shared by Part A line 2 (legal entity) and Part B line 4 (registering for UI yes/no), so only the legal entity is set; the UI Yes/No box is left for the signer to tick. The signature and its date are left for the signer.",
